window.SECTIONS=window.SECTIONS||[];window.SECTIONS.push({"id":"grammar","name":"Grammaire — mémo","short":"Mémo","color":"#3D6FB4","blurb":"A compact reference for être, avoir, the tenses and a few pronouns. The chapter-by-chapter course is under Grammaire progressive.","lessons":[{"id":"gm-conjugation","label":"Verb Conjugation","name":"Verb Conjugation","summary":"The system that ties the other Grammar lessons together: moods and tenses mapped out, which stem feeds which tense, full conjugation tables for a model verb from each group, être and avoir in full, reflexive verb mechanics, and the avoir/être auxiliary choice.","art":null,"bookpages":null,"groups":[{"name":"La carte d'ensemble : modes et temps","items":[["L'indicatif — le mode des faits","lan-dee-ka-TEEF","the indicative — the mood of facts and reality"],["le présent, le passé composé, l'imparfait, le plus-que-parfait, le futur proche, le futur simple","luh pray-ZAHN, luh pa-say kohm-po-ZAY, lan-par-FAY, luh plew-kuh-par-FAY","present, perfect, imperfect, pluperfect, near future, simple future — all indicative tenses"],["Le conditionnel — le mode de l'hypothèse et de la politesse","luh kohn-dee-see-o-NELL","the conditional — the mood of hypothesis and politeness"],["Le subjonctif — le mode du doute, du souhait, de l'obligation subjective","luh sewb-zhohnk-TEEF","the subjunctive — the mood of doubt, wish, subjective necessity"],["L'impératif — le mode de l'ordre et du conseil, sans sujet exprimé","lan-pay-ra-TEEF","the imperative — the mood of orders and advice, with no stated subject"],["L'infinitif et le participe — les formes non conjuguées, utilisées comme noms ou pour construire d'autres temps","lan-fee-nee-TEEF … luh par-tee-SEEP","the infinitive and participle — the unconjugated forms, used as nouns or to build other tenses"]],"note":"French organizes conjugation into <strong>modes</strong> (moods — the speaker's stance toward the action: fact, hypothesis, doubt, order) and, within the indicative, several <strong>temps</strong> (tenses — when it happens). This site's other Grammar lessons each cover one tense or mood in depth; this page is the map that shows how they fit together, plus the mechanics that cut across all of them."},{"name":"Le secret : quel radical pour quel temps ?","items":[["Le présent : pas de raccourci — le radical de chaque verbe s'apprend, groupe par groupe.","luh pray-ZAHN … luh ra-dee-KAL","The present has no shortcut — its stem is simply learned per verb group."],["L'imparfait : toujours le radical du présent avec NOUS, moins -ons, + terminaisons -ais/-ais/-ait/-ions/-iez/-aient.","lan-par-FAY … moins ohn","The imperfect always uses the present nous-stem, minus -ons, plus its own endings."],["Exemple : nous FINISSons → je finissais. Nous BUVons → je buvais. Seule exception : être → j'étais.","noo fee-nee-SOHN → zhuh fee-nee-SAY","finir → je finissais; boire → je buvais; être is the one true exception."],["Le futur simple et le conditionnel : le même radical pour les deux — en général l'infinitif complet (verbes en -er/-ir), ou l'infinitif moins -e (verbes en -re).","luh few-TEUR SANPL ay luh kohn-dee-see-o-NELL … lan-fee-nee-TEEF","Future and conditional share one stem — usually the whole infinitive, or the infinitive minus -e for -re verbs."],["Exemple : parler → je parlerai / je parlerais. Vendre → je vendrai / je vendrais.","par-LAY → zhuh par-luh-RAY / zhuh par-luh-RAY","parler → je parlerai / je parlerais; vendre → je vendrai / je vendrais."],["Le subjonctif présent : le radical du présent avec ILS, moins -ent, pour je/tu/il/ils ; le radical de l'imparfait (= nous du présent) pour nous/vous.","… luh ra-dee-KAL duh lan-par-FAY … poor NOO/VOO","Present subjunctive: the ils-stem of the present for most persons; the imparfait stem for nous/vous."],["Exemple : ils FINISSent → que je finisse. Nous FINISSons → que nous finissions.","eel fee-NEESS → kuh zhuh fee-NEESS","ils finissent → que je finisse; nous finissons → que nous finissions."],["Le passé composé et le plus-que-parfait : pas de radical du tout — un participe passé fixe, posé après avoir ou être conjugués.","luh pa-say kohm-po-ZAY … uhn par-tee-SEEP pa-SAY FEEKS","Passé composé and plus-que-parfait use no stem at all — a fixed past participle after a conjugated avoir or être."]],"note":"This is the single most useful pattern in French conjugation: almost every tense borrows its stem from somewhere else in the system rather than inventing a new one. Learn the present tense of a verb thoroughly, and the imparfait and subjonctif largely follow for free; learn the infinitive, and the futur and conditionnel follow for free."},{"name":"Parler — modèle complet, 1er groupe (-er)","items":[["Présent : je parle, tu parles, il/elle parle, nous parlons, vous parlez, ils/elles parlent","zhuh PARL, tew PARL, eel PARL, noo par-LOHN, voo par-LAY, eel PARL","I speak, you speak, he/she speaks, we speak, you speak, they speak"],["Passé composé : j'ai parlé, tu as parlé, il/elle a parlé, nous avons parlé, vous avez parlé, ils/elles ont parlé","zhay par-LAY, tew a par-LAY, ee la par-LAY, noo za-vohn par-LAY, voo za-vay par-LAY, eel zohn par-LAY","I spoke/have spoken, you spoke, he/she spoke, we spoke, you spoke, they spoke"],["Imparfait : je parlais, tu parlais, il/elle parlait, nous parlions, vous parliez, ils/elles parlaient","zhuh par-LAY, tew par-LAY, eel par-LAY, noo par-lee-OHN, voo par-lee-AY, eel par-LAY","I was speaking/used to speak (all six forms)"],["Plus-que-parfait : j'avais parlé, tu avais parlé, il/elle avait parlé, nous avions parlé, vous aviez parlé, ils/elles avaient parlé","zha-VAY par-LAY, tew a-VAY par-LAY, ee la-VAY par-LAY, noo za-vee-OHN par-LAY, voo za-vee-AY par-LAY, eel za-VAY par-LAY","I had spoken (all six forms)"],["Futur proche : je vais parler, tu vas parler, il/elle va parler, nous allons parler, vous allez parler, ils/elles vont parler","zhuh vay par-LAY, tew va par-LAY, eel va par-LAY, noo za-lohn par-LAY, voo za-lay par-LAY, eel vohn par-LAY","I'm going to speak (all six forms)"],["Futur simple : je parlerai, tu parleras, il/elle parlera, nous parlerons, vous parlerez, ils/elles parleront","zhuh par-luh-RAY, tew par-luh-RA, eel par-luh-RA, noo par-luh-ROHN, voo par-luh-RAY, eel par-luh-ROHN","I will speak (all six forms)"],["Conditionnel présent : je parlerais, tu parlerais, il/elle parlerait, nous parlerions, vous parleriez, ils/elles parleraient","zhuh par-luh-RAY, tew par-luh-RAY, eel par-luh-RAY, noo par-luh-ree-OHN, voo par-luh-ree-AY, eel par-luh-RAY","I would speak (all six forms)"],["Subjonctif présent : que je parle, que tu parles, qu'il/elle parle, que nous parlions, que vous parliez, qu'ils/elles parlent","kuh zhuh PARL, kuh tew PARL, keel PARL, kuh noo par-lee-OHN, kuh voo par-lee-AY, keel PARL","that I speak, that you speak… (all six forms)"],["Impératif : Parle ! Parlons ! Parlez !","PARL ! par-LOHN ! par-LAY !","Speak! Let's speak! Speak! (tu, nous, vous — no other persons exist in the imperative)"]],"note":"Notice how much of this table is built from just two pieces: the stem <strong>parl-</strong> and a small set of recurring endings. Once <em>parl-</em> is fixed, the imparfait, futur, conditionnel and subjonctif columns above are almost mechanical.","cols":"two"},{"name":"Comparer les trois groupes : présent, passé composé, imparfait, futur","items":[["1er groupe (-ER), ex. aimer — présent : j'aime, nous aimons, ils aiment","ZHEM, noo zay-MOHN, eel ZEM","1st group: I love, we love, they love"],["aimer — passé composé : j'ai aimé — imparfait : j'aimais — futur : j'aimerai","zhay ay-MAY … zhem-AY … zhem-RAY","1st group: I loved (all three past/future forms)"],["2e groupe (-IR, avec -iss-), ex. finir — présent : je finis, nous finissons, ils finissent","zhuh fee-NEE, noo fee-nee-SOHN, eel fee-NEESS","2nd group: I finish, we finish, they finish — the -iss- infix is the group's signature"],["finir — passé composé : j'ai fini — imparfait : je finissais — futur : je finirai","zhay fee-NEE … zhuh fee-nee-SAY … zhuh fee-nee-RAY","2nd group: I finished (all three past/future forms)"],["3e groupe (-RE régulier), ex. vendre — présent : je vends, nous vendons, ils vendent","zhuh VAHN, noo vahn-DOHN, eel VAHND","3rd group -re: I sell, we sell, they sell — note the singular has no ending at all"],["vendre — passé composé : j'ai vendu — imparfait : je vendais — futur : je vendrai","zhay vahn-DEW … zhuh vahn-DAY … zhuh vahn-DRAY","3rd group -re: I sold (all three past/future forms)"],["3e groupe irrégulier, ex. prendre — présent : je prends, nous prenons, ils prennent","zhuh PRAHN, noo pruh-NOHN, eel PREN","3rd group irregular: I take, we take, they take — the stem itself changes, not just the ending"],["prendre — passé composé : j'ai pris — imparfait : je prenais — futur : je prendrai","zhay PREE … zhuh pruh-NAY … zhuh prahn-DRAY","3rd group irregular: I took (all three past/future forms) — note the irregular participle pris"]],"note":"The 3rd group is really two different things wearing one label: <strong>regular -re verbs</strong> like vendre, which follow a predictable pattern, and a long tail of <strong>genuinely irregular verbs</strong> like prendre, where the stem itself shifts between singular and plural (je prends vs nous prenons) and the participle must simply be learned (pris, not 'prendu').","cols":"two"},{"name":"Être et avoir : les deux piliers du système","items":[["Être — présent : je suis, tu es, il/elle est, nous sommes, vous êtes, ils/elles sont","zhuh SWEE, tew AY, ee LAY, noo SOM, voo ZET, eel SOHN","I am, you are, he/she is, we are, you are, they are"],["Être — imparfait : j'étais, tu étais, il/elle était, nous étions, vous étiez, ils/elles étaient","zhay-TAY, tew ay-TAY, ee lay-TAY, noo zay-tee-OHN, voo zay-tee-AY, eel zay-TAY","I was (all six forms) — the one verb whose imparfait stem isn't the présent nous-stem"],["Être — futur simple : je serai, tu seras, il/elle sera, nous serons, vous serez, ils/elles seront","zhuh suh-RAY, tew suh-RA, eel suh-RA, noo suh-ROHN, voo suh-RAY, eel suh-ROHN","I will be (all six forms)"],["Être — subjonctif présent : que je sois, que tu sois, qu'il/elle soit, que nous soyons, que vous soyez, qu'ils/elles soient","kuh zhuh SWAH, kuh tew SWAH, keel SWAH, kuh noo swa-YOHN, kuh voo swa-YAY, keel SWAHT","that I be, that you be… (all six forms) — one of the few fully irregular subjonctifs"],["Avoir — présent : j'ai, tu as, il/elle a, nous avons, vous avez, ils/elles ont","ZHAY, tew A, ee LA, noo za-VOHN, voo za-VAY, eel ZOHN","I have, you have, he/she has, we have, you have, they have"],["Avoir — imparfait : j'avais, tu avais, il/elle avait, nous avions, vous aviez, ils/elles avaient","zha-VAY, tew a-VAY, ee la-VAY, noo za-vee-OHN, voo za-vee-AY, eel za-VAY","I had (all six forms)"],["Avoir — futur simple : j'aurai, tu auras, il/elle aura, nous aurons, vous aurez, ils/elles auront","zho-RAY, tew o-RA, ee lo-RA, noo zo-ROHN, voo zo-RAY, eel zo-ROHN","I will have (all six forms)"],["Avoir — subjonctif présent : que j'aie, que tu aies, qu'il/elle ait, que nous ayons, que vous ayez, qu'ils/elles aient","kuh ZHAY, kuh tew AY, kee LAY, kuh noo za-YOHN, kuh voo za-YAY, kee LAY","that I have, that you have… (all six forms) — the other fully irregular subjonctif"]],"note":"Être and avoir refuse almost every rule in the two groups above: their présent stems change shape by person, être's imparfait doesn't come from a nous-form, and both have unique subjonctif stems. There's no way around memorizing these two fully — but the payoff is enormous, since they're the auxiliary for every compound tense in the language.","cols":"two"},{"name":"Les verbes pronominaux : la mécanique du pronom réfléchi","items":[["Chaque personne a son propre pronom réfléchi : me, te, se, nous, vous, se — placé juste avant le verbe.","muh, tuh, suh, noo, voo, suh","my, your, him/herself, our, your, themselves — the reflexive pronoun set"],["Se lever — présent : je me lève, tu te lèves, il/elle se lève, nous nous levons, vous vous levez, ils/elles se lèvent","zhuh muh LEV, tew tuh LEV, eel suh LEV, noo noo luh-VOHN, voo voo luh-VAY, eel suh LEV","I get up, you get up… (all six forms)"],["Se lever — passé composé : je me suis levé(e), tu t'es levé(e), il s'est levé, elle s'est levée, nous nous sommes levé(e)s, vous vous êtes levé(e)(s), ils se sont levés, elles se sont levées","zhuh muh swee luh-VAY … eel suh sohn luh-VAY","I got up, you got up… — always with être, and the participle agrees with the reflexive pronoun"],["Négation au présent : je NE me lève PAS. Ne entoure le pronom + verbe ensemble.","zhuh nuh muh lev PAH","I don't get up — ne…pas wraps around the pronoun and verb as one block"],["Négation au passé composé : je NE me suis PAS levé(e). Ne entoure le pronom + l'auxiliaire.","zhuh nuh muh swee pah luh-VAY","I didn't get up — ne…pas wraps around the pronoun and the auxiliary être"],["Impératif affirmatif : Lève-toi ! Levons-nous ! Levez-vous ! — le pronom passe après le verbe, et te devient toi.","LEV-twah ! luh-VOHN-noo ! luh-VAY-voo !","Get up! Let's get up! Get up! — the pronoun moves after the verb, joined by a hyphen"],["Impératif négatif : Ne te lève pas ! Ne nous levons pas ! Ne vous levez pas ! — le pronom revient devant le verbe.","nuh tuh lev PAH ! nuh noo luh-vohn PAH !","Don't get up! Let's not get up! Don't get up! — the pronoun goes back in front"]],"note":"Reflexive verbs always take <strong>être</strong> in every compound tense, without exception — that part of the auxiliary choice is automatic. The only genuine decision left is the participle agreement, which follows the reflexive pronoun rather than the subject in most cases, though there are refinements beyond A1/A2 level (when the reflexive pronoun is a direct vs indirect object) that aren't covered here."},{"name":"Avoir ou être ? Le choix de l'auxiliaire pour les temps composés","items":[["Par défaut : AVOIR. La grande majorité des verbes français forment leurs temps composés avec avoir.","a-VWAHR","By default: avoir. Most French verbs use avoir for their compound tenses."],["Exception 1 — les verbes pronominaux : toujours ÊTRE, sans exception. Je me suis levé(e), ils se sont vus.","EH-truh","Exception 1 — reflexive verbs: always être, no exceptions."],["Exception 2 — un groupe fermé d'environ 15 verbes de mouvement ou de changement d'état : ÊTRE.","EH-truh","Exception 2 — a closed set of about 15 verbs of movement or change of state: être."],["Les paires classiques : aller/venir, arriver/partir, entrer/sortir, monter/descendre, naître/mourir.","a-LAY/vuh-NEER, a-ree-VAY/par-TEER, ahn-TRAY/sor-TEER, mohn-TAY/day-SAHN-druh, NET-ruh/moo-REER","the paired opposites — the easiest way to memorise the list"],["Les autres : rester, tomber, passer, retourner (et leurs composés : revenir, devenir, rentrer…).","res-TAY, tohm-BAY, pa-SAY, ruh-toor-NAY","the remaining être-verbs, plus their prefixed compounds"],["Accord avec être : le participe passé s'accorde avec le sujet — +e si féminin, +s si pluriel. Elle est partie. Ils sont partis. Elles sont parties.","el ay par-TEE. eel sohn par-TEE","Agreement with être: the past participle agrees with the subject in gender and number."],["Pas d'accord avec avoir : le participe passé reste invariable, quel que soit le sujet. Elle a mangé. Ils ont mangé.","el a mahn-ZHAY. eel zohn mahn-ZHAY","No agreement with avoir: the past participle never changes, whatever the subject."],["Ce même choix avoir/être sert pour TOUS les temps composés, pas seulement le passé composé : le plus-que-parfait suit exactly la même règle (j'avais parlé / j'étais parti(e)).","… luh plew-kuh-par-FAY sweet ek-zakt-MAHN lah mem REG","This same avoir/être choice governs every compound tense, not just the passé composé — the plus-que-parfait follows the identical rule."]],"note":"This choice is made once per verb and then applies everywhere that verb needs a compound tense — passé composé, plus-que-parfait, and beyond A2 level, the compound subjunctive and conditional too. Learn the auxiliary for a verb once, and it's settled for life."}]},{"id":"gm-verbs-regular","label":"Regular Verbs — Full Reference","name":"Regular Verbs — Full Reference","summary":"Every spelling-change pattern of the three regular verb groups, with 105 common verbs conjugated in full across all six persons in the present tense — enough to conjugate any regular French verb by analogy, since new verbs entering the language all follow one of these patterns.","art":null,"bookpages":null,"groups":[{"name":"1er groupe (-ER), radical inchangé — 35 verbes très courants","items":[["parler : je/j' parle, tu parles, il/elle parle, nous parlons, vous parlez, ils/elles parlent","PARL, PARL, PARL, par-LOHN, par-LAY, PARL","to speak"],["aimer : je/j' aime, tu aimes, il/elle aime, nous aimons, vous aimez, ils/elles aiment","EM, EM, EM, ay-MOHN, ay-MAY, EM","to like, love"],["habiter : je/j' habite, tu habites, il/elle habite, nous habitons, vous habitez, ils/elles habitent","a-BEET, a-BEET, a-BEET, a-bee-TOHN, a-bee-TAY, a-BEET","to live (somewhere)"],["travailler : je/j' travaille, tu travailles, il/elle travaille, nous travaillons, vous travaillez, ils/elles travaillent","tra-VIGH, tra-VIGH, tra-VIGH, tra-va-YOHN, tra-va-YAY, tra-VIGH","to work"],["regarder : je/j' regarde, tu regardes, il/elle regarde, nous regardons, vous regardez, ils/elles regardent","ruh-GARD, ruh-GARD, ruh-GARD, ruh-gar-DOHN, ruh-gar-DAY, ruh-GARD","to watch, look at"],["écouter : je/j' écoute, tu écoutes, il/elle écoute, nous écoutons, vous écoutez, ils/elles écoutent","ay-KOOT, ay-KOOT, ay-KOOT, ay-koo-TOHN, ay-koo-TAY, ay-KOOT","to listen"],["chanter : je/j' chante, tu chantes, il/elle chante, nous chantons, vous chantez, ils/elles chantent","SHAHNT, SHAHNT, SHAHNT, shahn-TOHN, shahn-TAY, SHAHNT","to sing"],["danser : je/j' danse, tu danses, il/elle danse, nous dansons, vous dansez, ils/elles dansent","DAHNSS, DAHNSS, DAHNSS, dahn-SOHN, dahn-SAY, DAHNSS","to dance"],["donner : je/j' donne, tu donnes, il/elle donne, nous donnons, vous donnez, ils/elles donnent","DUN, DUN, DUN, do-NOHN, do-NAY, DUN","to give"],["chercher : je/j' cherche, tu cherches, il/elle cherche, nous cherchons, vous cherchez, ils/elles cherchent","SHAIRSH, SHAIRSH, SHAIRSH, shair-SHOHN, shair-SHAY, SHAIRSH","to look for"],["trouver : je/j' trouve, tu trouves, il/elle trouve, nous trouvons, vous trouvez, ils/elles trouvent","TROOV, TROOV, TROOV, troo-VOHN, troo-VAY, TROOV","to find"],["arriver : je/j' arrive, tu arrives, il/elle arrive, nous arrivons, vous arrivez, ils/elles arrivent","a-REEV, a-REEV, a-REEV, a-ree-VOHN, a-ree-VAY, a-REEV","to arrive"],["penser : je/j' pense, tu penses, il/elle pense, nous pensons, vous pensez, ils/elles pensent","PAHNSS, PAHNSS, PAHNSS, pahn-SOHN, pahn-SAY, PAHNSS","to think"],["marcher : je/j' marche, tu marches, il/elle marche, nous marchons, vous marchez, ils/elles marchent","MARSH, MARSH, MARSH, mar-SHOHN, mar-SHAY, MARSH","to walk"],["jouer : je/j' joue, tu joues, il/elle joue, nous jouons, vous jouez, ils/elles jouent","ZHOO, ZHOO, ZHOO, zhoo-OHN, zhoo-AY, ZHOO","to play"],["aider : je/j' aide, tu aides, il/elle aide, nous aidons, vous aidez, ils/elles aident","ED, ED, ED, ay-DOHN, ay-DAY, ED","to help"],["demander : je/j' demande, tu demandes, il/elle demande, nous demandons, vous demandez, ils/elles demandent","duh-MAHND, duh-MAHND, duh-MAHND, duh-mahn-DOHN, duh-mahn-DAY, duh-MAHND","to ask (for)"],["dessiner : je/j' dessine, tu dessines, il/elle dessine, nous dessinons, vous dessinez, ils/elles dessinent","day-SEEN, day-SEEN, day-SEEN, day-see-NOHN, day-see-NAY, day-SEEN","to draw"],["laisser : je/j' laisse, tu laisses, il/elle laisse, nous laissons, vous laissez, ils/elles laissent","LESS, LESS, LESS, lay-SOHN, lay-SAY, LESS","to leave, let"],["montrer : je/j' montre, tu montres, il/elle montre, nous montrons, vous montrez, ils/elles montrent","MOHN-truh, MOHN-truh, MOHN-truh, mohn-TROHN, mohn-TRAY, MOHN-truh","to show"],["oublier : je/j' oublie, tu oublies, il/elle oublie, nous oublions, vous oubliez, ils/elles oublient","oo-BLEE, oo-BLEE, oo-BLEE, oo-blee-OHN, oo-blee-AY, oo-BLEE","to forget"],["porter : je/j' porte, tu portes, il/elle porte, nous portons, vous portez, ils/elles portent","PORT, PORT, PORT, por-TOHN, por-TAY, PORT","to wear, carry"],["préparer : je/j' prépare, tu prépares, il/elle prépare, nous préparons, vous préparez, ils/elles préparent","pray-PAR, pray-PAR, pray-PAR, pray-pa-ROHN, pray-pa-RAY, pray-PAR","to prepare"],["présenter : je/j' présente, tu présentes, il/elle présente, nous présentons, vous présentez, ils/elles présentent","pray-ZAHNT, pray-ZAHNT, pray-ZAHNT, pray-zahn-TOHN, pray-zahn-TAY, pray-ZAHNT","to introduce, present"],["quitter : je/j' quitte, tu quittes, il/elle quitte, nous quittons, vous quittez, ils/elles quittent","KEET, KEET, KEET, kee-TOHN, kee-TAY, KEET","to leave (a place/person)"],["rencontrer : je/j' rencontre, tu rencontres, il/elle rencontre, nous rencontrons, vous rencontrez, ils/elles rencontrent","rahn-KOHN-truh, rahn-KOHN-truh, rahn-KOHN-truh, rahn-kohn-TROHN, rahn-kohn-TRAY, rahn-KOHN-truh","to meet"],["rester : je/j' reste, tu restes, il/elle reste, nous restons, vous restez, ils/elles restent","REST, REST, REST, res-TOHN, res-TAY, REST","to stay"],["tourner : je/j' tourne, tu tournes, il/elle tourne, nous tournons, vous tournez, ils/elles tournent","TOORN, TOORN, TOORN, toor-NOHN, toor-NAY, TOORN","to turn"],["utiliser : je/j' utilise, tu utilises, il/elle utilise, nous utilisons, vous utilisez, ils/elles utilisent","ew-tee-LEEZ, ew-tee-LEEZ, ew-tee-LEEZ, ew-tee-lee-ZOHN, ew-tee-lee-ZAY, ew-tee-LEEZ","to use"],["visiter : je/j' visite, tu visites, il/elle visite, nous visitons, vous visitez, ils/elles visitent","vee-ZEET, vee-ZEET, vee-ZEET, vee-zee-TOHN, vee-zee-TAY, vee-ZEET","to visit (a place)"],["adorer : je/j' adore, tu adores, il/elle adore, nous adorons, vous adorez, ils/elles adorent","a-DOR, a-DOR, a-DOR, a-do-ROHN, a-do-RAY, a-DOR","to adore"],["détester : je/j' déteste, tu détestes, il/elle déteste, nous détestons, vous détestez, ils/elles détestent","day-TEST, day-TEST, day-TEST, day-tes-TOHN, day-tes-TAY, day-TEST","to hate"],["fermer : je/j' ferme, tu fermes, il/elle ferme, nous fermons, vous fermez, ils/elles ferment","FAIRM, FAIRM, FAIRM, fair-MOHN, fair-MAY, FAIRM","to close"],["gagner : je/j' gagne, tu gagnes, il/elle gagne, nous gagnons, vous gagnez, ils/elles gagnent","GAN-yuh, GAN-yuh, GAN-yuh, ga-NYOHN, ga-NYAY, GAN-yuh","to win, earn"],["inviter : je/j' invite, tu invites, il/elle invite, nous invitons, vous invitez, ils/elles invitent","an-VEET, an-VEET, an-VEET, an-vee-TOHN, an-vee-TAY, an-VEET","to invite"]],"note":"This is the largest verb family in French — around 90% of all verbs, and every new verb entering the language (télécharger, googliser…) joins it automatically. Once you know this pattern, you can conjugate any of the thousands of -er verbs not listed here."},{"name":"-GER : un e conservé devant -ons","items":[["manger : je/j' mange, tu manges, il/elle mange, nous mangeons, vous mangez, ils/elles mangent","MAHNZH, MAHNZH, MAHNZH, mahn-ZHOHN, mahn-ZHAY, MAHNZH","to eat"],["changer : je/j' change, tu changes, il/elle change, nous changeons, vous changez, ils/elles changent","SHAHNZH, SHAHNZH, SHAHNZH, shahn-ZHOHN, shahn-ZHAY, SHAHNZH","to change"],["voyager : je/j' voyage, tu voyages, il/elle voyage, nous voyageons, vous voyagez, ils/elles voyagent","vwa-YAHZH, vwa-YAHZH, vwa-YAHZH, vwa-ya-ZHOHN, vwa-ya-ZHAY, vwa-YAHZH","to travel"],["nager : je/j' nage, tu nages, il/elle nage, nous nageons, vous nagez, ils/elles nagent","NAHZH, NAHZH, NAHZH, na-ZHOHN, na-ZHAY, NAHZH","to swim"],["ranger : je/j' range, tu ranges, il/elle range, nous rangeons, vous rangez, ils/elles rangent","RAHNZH, RAHNZH, RAHNZH, rahn-ZHOHN, rahn-ZHAY, RAHNZH","to tidy"],["partager : je/j' partage, tu partages, il/elle partage, nous partageons, vous partagez, ils/elles partagent","par-TAHZH, par-TAHZH, par-TAHZH, par-ta-ZHOHN, par-ta-ZHAY, par-TAHZH","to share"],["bouger : je/j' bouge, tu bouges, il/elle bouge, nous bougeons, vous bougez, ils/elles bougent","BOOZH, BOOZH, BOOZH, boo-ZHOHN, boo-ZHAY, BOOZH","to move"],["plonger : je/j' plonge, tu plonges, il/elle plonge, nous plongeons, vous plongez, ils/elles plongent","PLOHNZH, PLOHNZH, PLOHNZH, plohn-ZHOHN, plohn-ZHAY, PLOHNZH","to dive"]],"note":"Only the nous form is unusual: <strong>mangeons</strong>, not 'mangons' — the extra e keeps the g soft (like the g in 'beige') before the o of -ons. Every other form is perfectly regular."},{"name":"-CER : une cédille devant -ons","items":[["commencer : je/j' commence, tu commences, il/elle commence, nous commençons, vous commencez, ils/elles commencent","ko-MAHNSS, ko-MAHNSS, ko-MAHNSS, ko-mahn-SOHN, ko-mahn-SAY, ko-MAHNSS","to begin"],["avancer : je/j' avance, tu avances, il/elle avance, nous avançons, vous avancez, ils/elles avancent","a-VAHNSS, a-VAHNSS, a-VAHNSS, a-vahn-SOHN, a-vahn-SAY, a-VAHNSS","to move forward"],["annoncer : je/j' annonce, tu annonces, il/elle annonce, nous annonçons, vous annoncez, ils/elles annoncent","a-NOHNSS, a-NOHNSS, a-NOHNSS, a-nohn-SOHN, a-nohn-SAY, a-NOHNSS","to announce"],["lancer : je/j' lance, tu lances, il/elle lance, nous lançons, vous lancez, ils/elles lancent","LAHNSS, LAHNSS, LAHNSS, lahn-SOHN, lahn-SAY, LAHNSS","to throw, launch"],["placer : je/j' place, tu places, il/elle place, nous plaçons, vous placez, ils/elles placent","PLAHSS, PLAHSS, PLAHSS, pla-SOHN, pla-SAY, PLAHSS","to place"],["prononcer : je/j' prononce, tu prononces, il/elle prononce, nous prononçons, vous prononcez, ils/elles prononcent","pro-NOHNSS, pro-NOHNSS, pro-NOHNSS, pro-nohn-SOHN, pro-nohn-SAY, pro-NOHNSS","to pronounce"]],"note":"Same idea as -ger, opposite fix: <strong>commençons</strong> takes a cedilla so the c stays soft (an 's' sound) before the o of -ons, instead of hardening to a 'k' sound."},{"name":"e + consonne + -er : l'accent grave apparaît","items":[["lever : je/j' lève, tu lèves, il/elle lève, nous levons, vous levez, ils/elles lèvent","LEV, LEV, LEV, luh-VOHN, luh-VAY, LEV","to lift, raise"],["acheter : je/j' achète, tu achètes, il/elle achète, nous achetons, vous achetez, ils/elles achètent","a-SHET, a-SHET, a-SHET, ash-TOHN, ash-TAY, a-SHET","to buy"],["amener : je/j' amène, tu amènes, il/elle amène, nous amenons, vous amenez, ils/elles amènent","a-MEN, a-MEN, a-MEN, am-NOHN, am-NAY, a-MEN","to bring (a person)"],["emmener : je/j' emmène, tu emmènes, il/elle emmène, nous emmenons, vous emmenez, ils/elles emmènent","ahm-MEN, ahm-MEN, ahm-MEN, ahm-NOHN, ahm-NAY, ahm-MEN","to take (a person) along"],["peser : je/j' pèse, tu pèses, il/elle pèse, nous pesons, vous pesez, ils/elles pèsent","PEZ, PEZ, PEZ, puh-ZOHN, puh-ZAY, PEZ","to weigh"]],"note":"Whenever the ending would be silent (je, tu, il, ils), the plain e of the stem opens to <strong>è</strong> so it can be heard at all — <em>je lève</em>, not 'je leve'. Before -ons/-ez, the ending itself carries the sound, so the e stays plain."},{"name":"-ELER / -ETER : la consonne double, pas d'accent","items":[["appeler : je/j' appelle, tu appelles, il/elle appelle, nous appelons, vous appelez, ils/elles appellent","a-PELL, a-PELL, a-PELL, a-play-OHN, a-play-AY, a-PELL","to call"],["jeter : je/j' jette, tu jettes, il/elle jette, nous jetons, vous jetez, ils/elles jettent","ZHET, ZHET, ZHET, zhuh-TOHN, zhuh-TAY, ZHET","to throw away"],["rappeler : je/j' rappelle, tu rappelles, il/elle rappelle, nous rappelons, vous rappelez, ils/elles rappellent","ra-PELL, ra-PELL, ra-PELL, ra-play-OHN, ra-play-AY, ra-PELL","to call back"],["épeler : je/j' épelle, tu épelles, il/elle épelle, nous épelons, vous épelez, ils/elles épellent","ay-PELL, ay-PELL, ay-PELL, ay-play-OHN, ay-play-AY, ay-PELL","to spell (a word)"]],"note":"A different fix for the same silent-ending problem: instead of adding an accent, these verbs <strong>double the consonant</strong> — <em>j'appelle</em> (two l's), <em>je jette</em> (two t's) — which has the same effect of opening the vowel sound. Note: modern spelling reform also allows acheter-style é-accent forms for some of these (j'appèle), but the doubled form remains standard."},{"name":"é + consonne + -er : é devient è devant une terminaison muette","items":[["préférer : je/j' préfère, tu préfères, il/elle préfère, nous préférons, vous préférez, ils/elles préfèrent","pray-FAIR, pray-FAIR, pray-FAIR, pray-fay-ROHN, pray-fay-RAY, pray-FAIR","to prefer"],["espérer : je/j' espère, tu espères, il/elle espère, nous espérons, vous espérez, ils/elles espèrent","es-PAIR, es-PAIR, es-PAIR, es-pay-ROHN, es-pay-RAY, es-PAIR","to hope"],["répéter : je/j' répète, tu répètes, il/elle répète, nous répétons, vous répétez, ils/elles répètent","ray-PET, ray-PET, ray-PET, ray-pay-TOHN, ray-pay-TAY, ray-PET","to repeat"],["célébrer : je/j' célèbre, tu célèbres, il/elle célèbre, nous célébrons, vous célébrez, ils/elles célèbrent","say-LEB-ruh, say-LEB-ruh, say-LEB-ruh, say-lay-BROHN, say-lay-BRAY, say-LEB-ruh","to celebrate"],["considérer : je/j' considère, tu considères, il/elle considère, nous considérons, vous considérez, ils/elles considèrent","kohn-see-DAIR, kohn-see-DAIR, kohn-see-DAIR, kohn-see-day-ROHN, kohn-see-day-RAY, kohn-see-DAIR","to consider"]],"note":"Same silent-ending logic again, this time on a stem that already has an accent: <strong>é → è</strong> — <em>je préfère</em>, not 'je préfére'. Unlike lever-type verbs, the nous/vous forms here keep the é unchanged, since -ons and -ez are pronounced clearly enough on their own."},{"name":"-YER : y devient i devant une terminaison muette","items":[["payer : je/j' paie, tu paies, il/elle paie, nous payons, vous payez, ils/elles paient","PAY, PAY, PAY, pay-YOHN, pay-YAY, PAY","to pay (also correct: je paye, tu payes… — both spellings are standard for -ayer verbs)"],["envoyer : je/j' envoie, tu envoies, il/elle envoie, nous envoyons, vous envoyez, ils/elles envoient","ahn-VWAH, ahn-VWAH, ahn-VWAH, ahn-vwa-YOHN, ahn-vwa-YAY, ahn-VWAH","to send"],["nettoyer : je/j' nettoie, tu nettoies, il/elle nettoie, nous nettoyons, vous nettoyez, ils/elles nettoient","net-TWAH, net-TWAH, net-TWAH, net-twa-YOHN, net-twa-YAY, net-TWAH","to clean"],["essayer : je/j' essaie, tu essaies, il/elle essaie, nous essayons, vous essayez, ils/elles essaient","ay-SAY, ay-SAY, ay-SAY, ay-say-YOHN, ay-say-YAY, ay-SAY","to try (also correct: j'essaye, tu essayes…)"],["employer : je/j' emploie, tu emploies, il/elle emploie, nous employons, vous employez, ils/elles emploient","ahm-PLWAH, ahm-PLWAH, ahm-PLWAH, ahm-plwa-YOHN, ahm-plwa-YAY, ahm-PLWAH","to use, employ"]],"note":"For -oyer and -uyer verbs this change is compulsory: <strong>j'envoie</strong>, never 'j'envoye'. For -ayer verbs (payer, essayer) both the y-form and the i-form are accepted in standard French, though the i-form is now more common in writing."},{"name":"2e groupe (-IR, avec -iss-) — 22 verbes courants","items":[["finir : je/j' finis, tu finis, il/elle finit, nous finissons, vous finissez, ils/elles finissent","fee-NEE, fee-NEE, fee-NEE, fee-nee-SOHN, fee-nee-SAY, fee-NEESS","to finish"],["choisir : je/j' choisis, tu choisis, il/elle choisit, nous choisissons, vous choisissez, ils/elles choisissent","shwa-ZEE, shwa-ZEE, shwa-ZEE, shwa-zee-SOHN, shwa-zee-SAY, shwa-ZEESS","to choose"],["réussir : je/j' réussis, tu réussis, il/elle réussit, nous réussissons, vous réussissez, ils/elles réussissent","ray-ew-SEE, ray-ew-SEE, ray-ew-SEE, ray-ew-see-SOHN, ray-ew-see-SAY, ray-ew-SEESS","to succeed"],["grandir : je/j' grandis, tu grandis, il/elle grandit, nous grandissons, vous grandissez, ils/elles grandissent","grahn-DEE, grahn-DEE, grahn-DEE, grahn-dee-SOHN, grahn-dee-SAY, grahn-DEESS","to grow"],["remplir : je/j' remplis, tu remplis, il/elle remplit, nous remplissons, vous remplissez, ils/elles remplissent","rahm-PLEE, rahm-PLEE, rahm-PLEE, rahm-plee-SOHN, rahm-plee-SAY, rahm-PLEESS","to fill"],["réfléchir : je/j' réfléchis, tu réfléchis, il/elle réfléchit, nous réfléchissons, vous réfléchissez, ils/elles réfléchissent","ray-flay-SHEE, ray-flay-SHEE, ray-flay-SHEE, ray-flay-shee-SOHN, ray-flay-shee-SAY, ray-flay-SHEESS","to think, reflect"],["rougir : je/j' rougis, tu rougis, il/elle rougit, nous rougissons, vous rougissez, ils/elles rougissent","roo-ZHEE, roo-ZHEE, roo-ZHEE, roo-zhee-SOHN, roo-zhee-SAY, roo-ZHEESS","to blush, turn red"],["vieillir : je/j' vieillis, tu vieillis, il/elle vieillit, nous vieillissons, vous vieillissez, ils/elles vieillissent","vee-ay-YEE, vee-ay-YEE, vee-ay-YEE, vee-ay-yee-SOHN, vee-ay-yee-SAY, vee-ay-YEESS","to grow old"],["maigrir : je/j' maigris, tu maigris, il/elle maigrit, nous maigrissons, vous maigrissez, ils/elles maigrissent","may-GREE, may-GREE, may-GREE, may-gree-SOHN, may-gree-SAY, may-GREESS","to lose weight"],["grossir : je/j' grossis, tu grossis, il/elle grossit, nous grossissons, vous grossissez, ils/elles grossissent","gro-SEE, gro-SEE, gro-SEE, gro-see-SOHN, gro-see-SAY, gro-SEESS","to gain weight"],["guérir : je/j' guéris, tu guéris, il/elle guérit, nous guérissons, vous guérissez, ils/elles guérissent","gay-REE, gay-REE, gay-REE, gay-ree-SOHN, gay-ree-SAY, gay-REESS","to heal, recover"],["obéir : je/j' obéis, tu obéis, il/elle obéit, nous obéissons, vous obéissez, ils/elles obéissent","o-bay-EE, o-bay-EE, o-bay-EE, o-bay-ee-SOHN, o-bay-ee-SAY, o-bay-EESS","to obey"],["punir : je/j' punis, tu punis, il/elle punit, nous punissons, vous punissez, ils/elles punissent","pew-NEE, pew-NEE, pew-NEE, pew-nee-SOHN, pew-nee-SAY, pew-NEESS","to punish"],["applaudir : je/j' applaudis, tu applaudis, il/elle applaudit, nous applaudissons, vous applaudissez, ils/elles applaudissent","a-plo-DEE, a-plo-DEE, a-plo-DEE, a-plo-dee-SOHN, a-plo-dee-SAY, a-plo-DEESS","to applaud"],["agir : je/j' agis, tu agis, il/elle agit, nous agissons, vous agissez, ils/elles agissent","a-ZHEE, a-ZHEE, a-ZHEE, a-zhee-SOHN, a-zhee-SAY, a-ZHEESS","to act"],["réagir : je/j' réagis, tu réagis, il/elle réagit, nous réagissons, vous réagissez, ils/elles réagissent","ray-a-ZHEE, ray-a-ZHEE, ray-a-ZHEE, ray-a-zhee-SOHN, ray-a-zhee-SAY, ray-a-ZHEESS","to react"],["établir : je/j' établis, tu établis, il/elle établit, nous établissons, vous établissez, ils/elles établissent","ay-ta-BLEE, ay-ta-BLEE, ay-ta-BLEE, ay-ta-blee-SOHN, ay-ta-blee-SAY, ay-ta-BLEESS","to establish"],["fournir : je/j' fournis, tu fournis, il/elle fournit, nous fournissons, vous fournissez, ils/elles fournissent","foor-NEE, foor-NEE, foor-NEE, foor-nee-SOHN, foor-nee-SAY, foor-NEESS","to supply"],["nourrir : je/j' nourris, tu nourris, il/elle nourrit, nous nourrissons, vous nourrissez, ils/elles nourrissent","noo-REE, noo-REE, noo-REE, noo-ree-SOHN, noo-ree-SAY, noo-REESS","to feed, nourish"],["avertir : je/j' avertis, tu avertis, il/elle avertit, nous avertissons, vous avertissez, ils/elles avertissent","a-vair-TEE, a-vair-TEE, a-vair-TEE, a-vair-tee-SOHN, a-vair-tee-SAY, a-vair-TEESS","to warn"],["bâtir : je/j' bâtis, tu bâtis, il/elle bâtit, nous bâtissons, vous bâtissez, ils/elles bâtissent","ba-TEE, ba-TEE, ba-TEE, ba-tee-SOHN, ba-tee-SAY, ba-TEESS","to build"],["saisir : je/j' saisis, tu saisis, il/elle saisit, nous saisissons, vous saisissez, ils/elles saisissent","say-ZEE, say-ZEE, say-ZEE, say-zee-SOHN, say-zee-SAY, say-ZEESS","to grab, seize"]],"note":"The signature of this whole family is the <strong>-iss-</strong> that appears in all three plural forms (nous finISSons, vous finISSez, ils finISSent) but nowhere in the singular. A much smaller group than the -er family, but every verb in it follows this one pattern with no exceptions."},{"name":"3e groupe régulier (-RE) — 14 verbes courants","items":[["vendre : je/j' vends, tu vends, il/elle vend, nous vendons, vous vendez, ils/elles vendent","VAHN, VAHN, VAHN, vahn-DOHN, vahn-DAY, VAHND","to sell"],["attendre : je/j' attends, tu attends, il/elle attend, nous attendons, vous attendez, ils/elles attendent","a-TAHN, a-TAHN, a-TAHN, a-tahn-DOHN, a-tahn-DAY, a-TAHND","to wait (for)"],["entendre : je/j' entends, tu entends, il/elle entend, nous entendons, vous entendez, ils/elles entendent","ahn-TAHN, ahn-TAHN, ahn-TAHN, ahn-tahn-DOHN, ahn-tahn-DAY, ahn-TAHND","to hear"],["descendre : je/j' descends, tu descends, il/elle descend, nous descendons, vous descendez, ils/elles descendent","day-SAHN, day-SAHN, day-SAHN, day-sahn-DOHN, day-sahn-DAY, day-SAHND","to go down"],["répondre : je/j' réponds, tu réponds, il/elle répond, nous répondons, vous répondez, ils/elles répondent","ray-POHN, ray-POHN, ray-POHN, ray-pohn-DOHN, ray-pohn-DAY, ray-POHND","to answer"],["perdre : je/j' perds, tu perds, il/elle perd, nous perdons, vous perdez, ils/elles perdent","PAIR, PAIR, PAIR, pair-DOHN, pair-DAY, PAIRD","to lose"],["rendre : je/j' rends, tu rends, il/elle rend, nous rendons, vous rendez, ils/elles rendent","RAHN, RAHN, RAHN, rahn-DOHN, rahn-DAY, RAHND","to give back"],["confondre : je/j' confonds, tu confonds, il/elle confond, nous confondons, vous confondez, ils/elles confondent","kohn-FOHN, kohn-FOHN, kohn-FOHN, kohn-fohn-DOHN, kohn-fohn-DAY, kohn-FOHND","to confuse, mix up"],["défendre : je/j' défends, tu défends, il/elle défend, nous défendons, vous défendez, ils/elles défendent","day-FAHN, day-FAHN, day-FAHN, day-fahn-DOHN, day-fahn-DAY, day-FAHND","to defend, forbid"],["dépendre : je/j' dépends, tu dépends, il/elle dépend, nous dépendons, vous dépendez, ils/elles dépendent","day-PAHN, day-PAHN, day-PAHN, day-pahn-DOHN, day-pahn-DAY, day-PAHND","to depend"],["tondre : je/j' tonds, tu tonds, il/elle tond, nous tondons, vous tondez, ils/elles tondent","TOHN, TOHN, TOHN, tohn-DOHN, tohn-DAY, TOHND","to mow"],["mordre : je/j' mords, tu mords, il/elle mord, nous mordons, vous mordez, ils/elles mordent","MOR, MOR, MOR, mor-DOHN, mor-DAY, MORD","to bite"],["tordre : je/j' tords, tu tords, il/elle tord, nous tordons, vous tordez, ils/elles tordent","TOR, TOR, TOR, tor-DOHN, tor-DAY, TORD","to twist"],["correspondre : je/j' corresponds, tu corresponds, il/elle correspond, nous correspondons, vous correspondez, ils/elles correspondent","ko-res-POHN, ko-res-POHN, ko-res-POHN, ko-res-pohn-DOHN, ko-res-pohn-DAY, ko-res-POHND","to correspond, match"]],"note":"This family's signature: the singular has <strong>no ending sound at all</strong> beyond the stem's own final consonant — je vends, tu vends, il vend all sound identical. The nous/vous/ils forms then add the ordinary -ons/-ez/-ent. Every one of these verbs takes -u in the past participle (vendu, perdu, répondu…)."}]},{"id":"gm-verbs-irregular","label":"Irregular Verbs — Full Reference","name":"Irregular Verbs — Full Reference","summary":"The complete standard set of French irregular verbs, organised by family, each with full present-tense conjugation across all six persons plus its past participle and auxiliary — with every compound verb in the family named alongside it.","art":null,"bookpages":null,"groups":[{"name":"Être, avoir, aller","items":[["être : je/j' suis, tu es, il/elle est, nous sommes, vous êtes, ils/elles sont — participe passé : été (avoir)","SWEE, AY, AY, SOM, ZET, SOHN","to be. Fully conjugated across every tense in the Verb Conjugation lesson above."],["avoir : je/j' ai, tu as, il/elle a, nous avons, vous avez, ils/elles ont — participe passé : eu (avoir)","AY, AH, AH, a-VOHN, a-VAY, OHN","to have. Fully conjugated across every tense in the Verb Conjugation lesson above."],["aller : je/j' vais, tu vas, il/elle va, nous allons, vous allez, ils/elles vont — participe passé : allé (être)","VAY, VAH, VAH, a-LOHN, a-LAY, VOHN","to go"]]},{"name":"Faire et sa famille","items":[["faire : je/j' fais, tu fais, il/elle fait, nous faisons, vous faites, ils/elles font — participe passé : fait (avoir)","FAY, FAY, FAY, fuh-ZOHN, FET, FOHN","to do, make. Conjugated the same way: défaire (to undo), refaire (to redo), satisfaire (to satisfy)"]],"note":"Two irregular sounds to fix in memory: <strong>nous faisons</strong> is pronounced 'fuh-zohn', not 'fay-zohn' — the only verb in French where <em>ai</em> sounds like <em>uh</em>. And <strong>vous faites</strong> is one of just three verbs (with être and dire) whose vous-form ends in -tes."},{"name":"Dire et sa famille","items":[["dire : je/j' dis, tu dis, il/elle dit, nous disons, vous dites, ils/elles disent — participe passé : dit (avoir)","DEE, DEE, DEE, dee-ZOHN, DEET, DEEZ","to say, tell. Conjugated the same way: redire (to say again). Exception within the family: contredire, interdire, prédire and médire use vous …disez (contredisez, interdisez) instead of dites."]]},{"name":"Savoir, pouvoir, vouloir, devoir — les quatre modaux","items":[["savoir : je/j' sais, tu sais, il/elle sait, nous savons, vous savez, ils/elles savent — participe passé : su (avoir)","SAY, SAY, SAY, sa-VOHN, sa-VAY, SAHV","to know (a fact, how to)"],["pouvoir : je/j' peux, tu peux, il/elle peut, nous pouvons, vous pouvez, ils/elles peuvent — participe passé : pu (avoir)","PUH, PUH, PUH, poo-VOHN, poo-VAY, PUV","to be able to, can. In inversion, je peux becomes puis-je ? (puis-je vous aider ?)"],["vouloir : je/j' veux, tu veux, il/elle veut, nous voulons, vous voulez, ils/elles veulent — participe passé : voulu (avoir)","VUH, VUH, VUH, voo-LOHN, voo-LAY, VUL","to want"],["devoir : je/j' dois, tu dois, il/elle doit, nous devons, vous devez, ils/elles doivent — participe passé : dû (avoir)","DWAH, DWAH, DWAH, duh-VOHN, duh-VAY, DWAHV","to have to, must; to owe. The circumflex on dû appears only in the masculine singular participle — due, dus, dues have none."]]},{"name":"Venir et tenir — deux grandes familles jumelles","items":[["venir : je/j' viens, tu viens, il/elle vient, nous venons, vous venez, ils/elles viennent — participe passé : venu (être)","vee-AN, vee-AN, vee-AN, vuh-NOHN, vuh-NAY, vee-EN","to come. Conjugated the same way, also with être: revenir (to come back), devenir (to become), parvenir (to reach, manage to), se souvenir (to remember, reflexive), prévenir (to warn — takes avoir), convenir (to suit — takes avoir)"],["tenir : je/j' tiens, tu tiens, il/elle tient, nous tenons, vous tenez, ils/elles tiennent — participe passé : tenu (avoir)","tee-AN, tee-AN, tee-AN, tuh-NOHN, tuh-NAY, tee-EN","to hold. Conjugated exactly like venir, but takes avoir. Same pattern: retenir (to hold back/remember), obtenir (to obtain), appartenir (to belong), contenir (to contain), maintenir (to maintain), entretenir (to maintain, look after)"]],"note":"Identical présent-tense pattern for both families — the nasal singular (viens/tiens) opening to a double-n plural (viennent/tiennent) — but they split on auxiliary: <strong>venir</strong>'s family takes être, <strong>tenir</strong>'s family takes avoir."},{"name":"Prendre et sa famille","items":[["prendre : je/j' prends, tu prends, il/elle prend, nous prenons, vous prenez, ils/elles prennent — participe passé : pris (avoir)","PRAHN, PRAHN, PRAHN, pruh-NOHN, pruh-NAY, PREN","to take. Conjugated the same way: apprendre (to learn), comprendre (to understand), surprendre (to surprise), reprendre (to take back, resume)"]]},{"name":"Mettre et sa famille","items":[["mettre : je/j' mets, tu mets, il/elle met, nous mettons, vous mettez, ils/elles mettent — participe passé : mis (avoir)","MAY, MAY, MAY, muh-TOHN, muh-TAY, MET","to put, place. Conjugated the same way: permettre (to allow), promettre (to promise), remettre (to hand over, postpone), admettre (to admit), soumettre (to submit)"]]},{"name":"Voir et sa famille","items":[["voir : je/j' vois, tu vois, il/elle voit, nous voyons, vous voyez, ils/elles voient — participe passé : vu (avoir)","VWAH, VWAH, VWAH, vwa-YOHN, vwa-YAY, VWAH","to see. Conjugated the same way: revoir (to see again), prévoir (to foresee, plan — note: its futur/conditionnel is irregular, je prévoirai, unlike voir's je verrai)"]]},{"name":"Écrire et sa famille","items":[["écrire : je/j' écris, tu écris, il/elle écrit, nous écrivons, vous écrivez, ils/elles écrivent — participe passé : écrit (avoir)","ay-KREE, ay-KREE, ay-KREE, ay-kree-VOHN, ay-kree-VAY, ay-KREEV","to write. Conjugated the same way: décrire (to describe), inscrire/s'inscrire (to enrol, register), prescrire (to prescribe), transcrire (to transcribe)"]]},{"name":"Lire et sa famille","items":[["lire : je/j' lis, tu lis, il/elle lit, nous lisons, vous lisez, ils/elles lisent — participe passé : lu (avoir)","LEE, LEE, LEE, lee-ZOHN, lee-ZAY, LEEZ","to read. Conjugated the same way: relire (to reread), élire (to elect)"]]},{"name":"Connaître et sa famille","items":[["connaître : je/j' connais, tu connais, il/elle connaît, nous connaissons, vous connaissez, ils/elles connaissent — participe passé : connu (avoir)","ko-NAY, ko-NAY, ko-NAY, ko-nay-SOHN, ko-nay-SAY, ko-NESS","to know (a person, a place). Conjugated the same way: reconnaître (to recognise), paraître (to seem, appear), apparaître (to appear), disparaître (to disappear)"]],"note":"Watch for the circumflex: it appears only where the stem is directly followed by a t — connaît, paraît — but not in the plural (connaissons) or the participle (connu)."},{"name":"Naître, mourir, boire, croire — quatre verbes uniques","items":[["naître : je/j' nais, tu nais, il/elle naît, nous naissons, vous naissez, ils/elles naissent — participe passé : né (être)","NAY, NAY, NAY, nay-SOHN, nay-SAY, NESS","to be born"],["mourir : je/j' meurs, tu meurs, il/elle meurt, nous mourons, vous mourez, ils/elles meurent — participe passé : mort (être)","MUR, MUR, MUR, moo-ROHN, moo-RAY, MUR","to die"],["boire : je/j' bois, tu bois, il/elle boit, nous buvons, vous buvez, ils/elles boivent — participe passé : bu (avoir)","BWAH, BWAH, BWAH, bew-VOHN, bew-VAY, BWAHV","to drink"],["croire : je/j' crois, tu crois, il/elle croit, nous croyons, vous croyez, ils/elles croient — participe passé : cru (avoir)","KRWAH, KRWAH, KRWAH, krwa-YOHN, krwa-YAY, KRWAH","to believe"]]},{"name":"Courir et sa famille","items":[["courir : je/j' cours, tu cours, il/elle court, nous courons, vous courez, ils/elles courent — participe passé : couru (avoir)","KOOR, KOOR, KOOR, koo-ROHN, koo-RAY, KOOR","to run. Conjugated the same way: parcourir (to travel across), secourir (to rescue)"]]},{"name":"Recevoir et sa famille","items":[["recevoir : je/j' reçois, tu reçois, il/elle reçoit, nous recevons, vous recevez, ils/elles reçoivent — participe passé : reçu (avoir)","ruh-SWAH, ruh-SWAH, ruh-SWAH, ruh-suh-VOHN, ruh-suh-VAY, ruh-SWAHV","to receive. Conjugated the same way: apercevoir (to glimpse), décevoir (to disappoint), concevoir (to conceive, design)"]],"note":"The cedilla in reçois/reçoit/reçoivent does the same job as in commençons — keeping the c soft before o."},{"name":"Dormir et sa famille","items":[["dormir : je/j' dors, tu dors, il/elle dort, nous dormons, vous dormez, ils/elles dorment — participe passé : dormi (avoir)","DOR, DOR, DOR, dor-MOHN, dor-MAY, DORM","to sleep. Conjugated the same way: s'endormir (to fall asleep — reflexive, takes être), redormir (to sleep again)"]]},{"name":"Partir, sortir, sentir — la famille qui perd sa consonne finale","items":[["partir : je/j' pars, tu pars, il/elle part, nous partons, vous partez, ils/elles partent — participe passé : parti (être)","PAR, PAR, PAR, par-TOHN, par-TAY, PART","to leave"],["sortir : je/j' sors, tu sors, il/elle sort, nous sortons, vous sortez, ils/elles sortent — participe passé : sorti (être)","SOR, SOR, SOR, sor-TOHN, sor-TAY, SORT","to go out"],["sentir : je/j' sens, tu sens, il/elle sent, nous sentons, vous sentez, ils/elles sentent — participe passé : senti (avoir)","SAHN, SAHN, SAHN, sahn-TOHN, sahn-TAY, SAHNT","to feel, smell. Same family: ressentir (to feel, experience — avoir), mentir (to lie — avoir): mens, mens, ment, mentons, mentez, mentent; se repentir (to repent — être)"]],"note":"These verbs drop the stem's final consonant in all three singular forms — <strong>je pars</strong>, not 'je part-s' — then restore it in the plural: nous partons. Compare this with dormir just above, which keeps its m throughout (je dors, not 'je dos') — the two families look similar but behave slightly differently."},{"name":"Servir et sa famille","items":[["servir : je/j' sers, tu sers, il/elle sert, nous servons, vous servez, ils/elles servent — participe passé : servi (avoir)","SAIR, SAIR, SAIR, sair-VOHN, sair-VAY, SAIRV","to serve. Conjugated the same way: desservir (to clear the table; to serve badly)"]]},{"name":"Ouvrir et sa famille — des -IR qui se conjuguent comme des -ER","items":[["ouvrir : je/j' ouvre, tu ouvres, il/elle ouvre, nous ouvrons, vous ouvrez, ils/elles ouvrent — participe passé : ouvert (avoir)","OO-vruh, OO-vruh, OO-vruh, oo-VROHN, oo-VRAY, OO-vruh","to open"],["offrir : je/j' offre, tu offres, il/elle offre, nous offrons, vous offrez, ils/elles offrent — participe passé : offert (avoir)","O-fruh, O-fruh, O-fruh, o-FROHN, o-FRAY, O-fruh","to offer, give (a gift)"],["couvrir : je/j' couvre, tu couvres, il/elle couvre, nous couvrons, vous couvrez, ils/elles couvrent — participe passé : couvert (avoir)","KOO-vruh, KOO-vruh, KOO-vruh, koo-VROHN, koo-VRAY, KOO-vruh","to cover. Also: découvrir (to discover) — découvert; souffrir (to suffer) — souffert"]],"note":"A trap worth knowing by name: despite the -ir infinitive, this whole family takes the <strong>-er verb endings</strong> in the present tense — j'ouvre, tu ouvres, not 'j'ouvris'. Only the participle (ouvert, offert, couvert…) reveals the irregularity."},{"name":"Suivre et sa famille","items":[["suivre : je/j' suis, tu suis, il/elle suit, nous suivons, vous suivez, ils/elles suivent — participe passé : suivi (avoir)","SWEE, SWEE, SWEE, swee-VOHN, swee-VAY, SWEEV","to follow. Conjugated the same way: poursuivre (to pursue, continue)"]],"note":"Fair warning: je suis from suivre is spelled and pronounced exactly like je suis from être. Only the rest of the sentence tells you which verb is meant."},{"name":"Vivre et sa famille","items":[["vivre : je/j' vis, tu vis, il/elle vit, nous vivons, vous vivez, ils/elles vivent — participe passé : vécu (avoir)","VEE, VEE, VEE, vee-VOHN, vee-VAY, VEEV","to live. Conjugated the same way: survivre (to survive)"]]},{"name":"Rire et sa famille","items":[["rire : je/j' ris, tu ris, il/elle rit, nous rions, vous riez, ils/elles rient — participe passé : ri (avoir)","REE, REE, REE, ree-OHN, ree-AY, REE","to laugh. Conjugated the same way: sourire (to smile)"]]},{"name":"Conduire et sa grande famille","items":[["conduire : je/j' conduis, tu conduis, il/elle conduit, nous conduisons, vous conduisez, ils/elles conduisent — participe passé : conduit (avoir)","kohn-DWEE, kohn-DWEE, kohn-DWEE, kohn-dwee-ZOHN, kohn-dwee-ZAY, kohn-DWEEZ","to drive, lead. Conjugated the same way: construire (to build), traduire (to translate), produire (to produce), détruire (to destroy), réduire (to reduce), séduire (to seduce)"]]},{"name":"Craindre et sa grande famille (-eindre, -aindre, -oindre)","items":[["craindre : je/j' crains, tu crains, il/elle craint, nous craignons, vous craignez, ils/elles craignent — participe passé : craint (avoir)","KRAN, KRAN, KRAN, kray-NYOHN, kray-NYAY, KRAN-yuh","to fear. Same pattern: plaindre/se plaindre (to pity/to complain), éteindre (to switch off) — éteins, éteint, éteignons…, peindre (to paint) — peins, peint, peignons…, joindre/rejoindre (to join), atteindre (to reach) — atteins, atteint, atteignons…"]],"note":"One consistent shape across this whole family: a nasal vowel in the singular (crains, peins, joins) that opens into <strong>-gn-</strong> in the plural (craignons, peignons, joignons) — never a plain n."},{"name":"S'asseoir, falloir, pleuvoir — trois cas à part","items":[["s'asseoir : je/j' m'assieds, tu t'assieds, il/elle s'assied, nous nous asseyons, vous vous asseyez, ils/elles s'asseyent — participe passé : assis (être)","ma-SYAY, ta-SYAY, sa-SYAY, noo za-say-YOHN, voo za-say-YAY, sa-SAY","to sit down. A second full set of forms is equally correct: je m'assois, tu t'assois, il s'assoit, nous nous assoyons, vous vous assoyez, ils s'assoient — both patterns are taught in French schools."],["falloir : je/j' -, tu -, il/elle il faut, nous -, vous -, ils/elles - — participe passé : fallu (avoir)","—, —, eel FOH, —, —, —","to be necessary (impersonal — only exists as il faut). Past: il a fallu. This verb has no je/tu/nous/vous/ils forms at all — it only ever takes il."],["pleuvoir : je/j' -, tu -, il/elle il pleut, nous -, vous -, ils/elles - — participe passé : plu (avoir)","—, —, eel PLUH, —, —, —","to rain (impersonal — only exists as il pleut). Past: il a plu. Like falloir, this verb only ever takes il, describing the weather."]]},{"name":"Plaire et se taire","items":[["plaire : je/j' plais, tu plais, il/elle plaît, nous plaisons, vous plaisez, ils/elles plaisent — participe passé : plu (avoir)","PLAY, PLAY, PLAY, play-ZOHN, play-ZAY, PLEZ","to please (ça me plaît = I like it). Same family: déplaire (to displease)"],["se taire : je/j' me tais, tu te tais, il/elle se tait, nous nous taisons, vous vous taisez, ils/elles se taisent — participe passé : tu (être)","muh TAY, tuh TAY, suh TAY, noo tay-ZOHN, voo tay-ZAY, suh TEZ","to fall silent, keep quiet. Conjugated like plaire but without the circumflex (il se tait, not 'se taît'), and reflexive with être"]]},{"name":"Résoudre, battre, vaincre — trois familles de plus","items":[["résoudre : je/j' résous, tu résous, il/elle résout, nous résolvons, vous résolvez, ils/elles résolvent — participe passé : résolu (avoir)","ray-ZOO, ray-ZOO, ray-ZOO, ray-zol-VOHN, ray-zol-VAY, ray-ZOLV","to solve, resolve"],["battre : je/j' bats, tu bats, il/elle bat, nous battons, vous battez, ils/elles battent — participe passé : battu (avoir)","BAH, BAH, BAH, ba-TOHN, ba-TAY, BAHT","to beat, hit. Conjugated the same way: combattre (to fight), abattre (to knock down)"],["vaincre : je/j' vaincs, tu vaincs, il/elle vainc, nous vainquons, vous vainquez, ils/elles vainquent — participe passé : vaincu (avoir)","VAN, VAN, VAN, van-KOHN, van-KAY, VANK","to defeat. Conjugated the same way: convaincre (to convince)"]]},{"name":"Acquérir, valoir, vêtir — les derniers de la liste","items":[["acquérir : je/j' acquiers, tu acquiers, il/elle acquiert, nous acquérons, vous acquérez, ils/elles acquièrent — participe passé : acquis (avoir)","a-kee-AIR, a-kee-AIR, a-kee-AIR, a-kay-ROHN, a-kay-RAY, a-kee-AIR","to acquire. Conjugated the same way: conquérir (to conquer)"],["valoir : je/j' vaux, tu vaux, il/elle vaut, nous valons, vous valez, ils/elles valent — participe passé : valu (avoir)","VOH, VOH, VOH, va-LOHN, va-LAY, VAHL","to be worth"],["vêtir : je/j' vêts, tu vêts, il/elle vêt, nous vêtons, vous vêtez, ils/elles vêtent — participe passé : vêtu (avoir)","VET, VET, VET, vay-TOHN, vay-TAY, VET","to dress, clothe (formal/literary). Rare outside set phrases like se vêtir, être vêtu de noir"]]}]},{"id":"gm-etre","label":"Le verbe","name":"Être — to be","art":"etretable","summary":"The single most used verb in French. Present tense in full, what it is for, the traps, and the fixed expressions built on it.","groups":[{"name":"Le présent","cols":"two","items":[["je suis","zhuh SWEE","I am"],["tu es","tew AY","you are (familiar)"],["il est","eel AY","he is"],["elle est","el AY","she is"],["on est","oh NAY","one is / we are"],["nous sommes","noo SUM","we are"],["vous êtes","voo ZET","you are (polite / plural)"],["ils sont","eel SOHN","they are (m)"],["elles sont","el SOHN","they are (f)"]]},{"name":"Ce qu'il faut entendre","note":"<strong>vous êtes</strong> has a liaison — voo-<strong>Z</strong>ET, never voo-ETT. And <strong>on est</strong> links too: oh-<strong>N</strong>AY.<br><br>The killer pair: <strong>ils sont</strong> (eel SOHN, they are) versus <strong>ils ont</strong> (eel ZOHN, they have). One z decides the meaning.","items":[["ils sont français","eel sohn frahn-SAY","they are French — s sound"],["ils ont un rêve","eel zohn tuhn REV","they have a dream — z sound"],["vous êtes prêt ?","voo ZET PREH","are you ready?"],["on est fatigué","oh nay fa-tee-GAY","we're tired"]]},{"name":"À quoi sert être","cols":"two","items":[["Je suis canadien.","zhuh swee ka-na-dee-AN","nationality"],["Je suis médecin.","zhuh swee mayd-SAN","job — no article, ever"],["Je suis grand.","zhuh swee GRAHN","description"],["Je suis fatigué.","zhuh swee fa-tee-GAY","state, how you feel"],["Je suis à Paris.","zhuh swee za pa-REE","where you are"],["Je suis marié.","zhuh swee ma-ree-AY","situation"],["C'est un bon restaurant.","set uhn bohn res-to-RAHN","identifying something"],["Il est trois heures.","eel ay trwa ZUR","telling the time"]]},{"name":"La négation et la question","cols":"two","items":[["Je ne suis pas français.","zhuh nuh swee pah frahn-SAY","I'm not French."],["Il n'est pas là.","eel nay pah LAH","He isn't here."],["Nous ne sommes pas prêts.","noo nuh som pah PREH","We're not ready."],["Vous êtes étudiant ?","voo ZET zay-tew-dee-AHN","Are you a student?"],["Est-ce que vous êtes marié ?","es-kuh voo ZET ma-ree-AY","Are you married?"],["Êtes-vous français ?","et VOO frahn-SAY","Are you French? — formal inversion"]]},{"name":"Les expressions avec être","cols":"two","items":[["être en retard","EH-truh ahn ruh-TAR","to be late"],["être à l'heure","EH-truh a LUR","to be on time"],["être en avance","EH-truh ah na-VAHNSS","to be early"],["être d'accord","EH-truh da-KOR","to agree"],["être en train de…","EH-truh ahn tran duh","to be in the middle of…"],["être en vacances","EH-truh ahn va-KAHNSS","to be on holiday"],["être libre","EH-truh LEE-bruh","to be free / available"],["être content de","EH-truh kohn-TAHN duh","to be pleased to"],["c'est / ce sont","SAY / suh SOHN","it is / they are"],["il est / elle est","eel AY / el AY","he is / she is"]]},{"name":"Le piège numéro un","note":"English says <em>I <strong>am</strong> hungry, I <strong>am</strong> 25, I <strong>am</strong> cold</em>. French uses <strong>avoir</strong> for all three. Saying <em>je suis faim</em> or <em>je suis 25 ans</em> is the classic beginner mistake.","items":[["J'ai faim.","zhay FAN","I'm hungry. — not je suis faim"],["J'ai 25 ans.","zhay van-sank AHN","I'm 25. — not je suis 25"],["J'ai froid.","zhay FRWAH","I'm cold. — not je suis froid"]]}]},{"id":"gm-avoir","label":"Le verbe","name":"Avoir — to have","art":"avoirtable","summary":"The other verb you cannot do without. Present tense, the liaisons that carry the meaning, and the long list of things French 'has' where English 'is'.","groups":[{"name":"Le présent","cols":"two","items":[["j'ai","ZHAY","I have"],["tu as","tew AH","you have"],["il a","ee LAH","he has"],["elle a","el LAH","she has"],["on a","oh NAH","one has / we have"],["nous avons","noo za-VOHN","we have"],["vous avez","voo za-VAY","you have"],["ils ont","eel ZOHN","they have (m)"],["elles ont","el ZOHN","they have (f)"]]},{"name":"Les liaisons d'avoir","note":"Every plural form of <em>avoir</em> starts with a vowel, so every one of them liaises: nou<strong>s a</strong>vons, vou<strong>s a</strong>vez, il<strong>s o</strong>nt — all with a <strong>z</strong>.","items":[["nous avons","noo za-VOHN","we have"],["vous avez","voo za-VAY","you have"],["ils ont / elles ont","eel ZOHN / el ZOHN","they have"],["il a un frère","ee la uhn FRAIR","he has a brother"],["on a une question","oh na ewn kes-tee-OHN","we have a question"]]},{"name":"Avoir pour l'âge et le corps","cols":"two","note":"These are all <strong>avoir</strong> in French and <strong>be</strong> in English. Learn them as a block.","items":[["avoir … ans","a-VWAHR … AHN","to be … years old"],["Quel âge avez-vous ? — J'ai trente ans.","kel AHZH a-vay VOO — zhay trahnt AHN","How old are you? — I'm thirty."],["avoir faim","a-VWAHR FAN","to be hungry"],["avoir soif","a-VWAHR SWAHF","to be thirsty"],["avoir chaud","a-VWAHR SHOW","to be hot"],["avoir froid","a-VWAHR FRWAH","to be cold"],["avoir sommeil","a-VWAHR so-MAY","to be sleepy"],["avoir peur","a-VWAHR PUR","to be afraid"],["avoir mal à…","a-VWAHR mal a","to have a pain in…"],["avoir raison","a-VWAHR ray-ZOHN","to be right"],["avoir tort","a-VWAHR TOR","to be wrong"],["avoir besoin de","a-VWAHR buh-ZWAN duh","to need"],["avoir envie de","a-VWAHR ahn-VEE duh","to feel like"],["avoir de la chance","a-VWAHR duh lah SHAHNSS","to be lucky"]]},{"name":"La négation — et le piège du « de »","note":"After a negative, <strong>un, une, des</strong> all collapse into <strong>de</strong> (or <strong>d'</strong>). <em>J'ai une voiture</em> → <em>Je n'ai <strong>pas de</strong> voiture</em>. This does not happen with <em>le, la, les</em>.","items":[["J'ai un frère. → Je n'ai pas de frère.","zhuh nay pah duh FRAIR","un → de"],["J'ai une voiture. → Je n'ai pas de voiture.","zhuh nay pah duh vwa-TEWR","une → de"],["J'ai des amis ici. → Je n'ai pas d'amis ici.","zhuh nay pah da-MEE ee-SEE","des → d'"],["Il n'a pas le temps.","eel na pah luh TAHN","le stays le"]]},{"name":"Il y a — there is, there are","note":"Built from <em>avoir</em> and completely fixed: <strong>il y a</strong> never changes for singular or plural.","items":[["Il y a un musée.","eel ya uhn mew-ZAY","There is a museum."],["Il y a des jardins.","eel ya day zhar-DAN","There are gardens."],["Il n'y a pas de pharmacie.","eel nya pah duh far-ma-SEE","There is no pharmacy."],["Qu'est-ce qu'il y a ?","kes-keel YA","What is there? / What's wrong?"],["Il y a combien de places ?","eel ya kohm-bee-AN duh PLAHSS","How many seats are there?"]]}]},{"id":"gm-poss","label":"Les déterminants","name":"L'adjectif possessif","art":"possessifs","summary":"mon, ma, mes… The rule that catches everyone: the word agrees with the thing owned, not with the owner.","groups":[{"name":"Le tableau complet","cols":"two","note":"Read across: <strong>masculine · feminine · plural</strong>. The choice depends entirely on the <em>noun that follows</em>.","items":[["mon frère · ma sœur · mes parents","mohn FRAIR · ma SUR · may pa-RAHN","my"],["ton frère · ta sœur · tes parents","tohn FRAIR · ta SUR · tay pa-RAHN","your (familiar)"],["son frère · sa sœur · ses parents","sohn FRAIR · sa SUR · say pa-RAHN","his / her / its"],["notre frère · notre sœur · nos parents","NOT-ruh · NOT-ruh · no pa-RAHN","our"],["votre frère · votre sœur · vos parents","VOT-ruh · VOT-ruh · vo pa-RAHN","your (polite / plural)"],["leur frère · leur sœur · leurs parents","lur FRAIR · lur SUR · lur pa-RAHN","their"]]},{"name":"Le point qui piège tout le monde","note":"<strong>son</strong> and <strong>sa</strong> do NOT tell you the owner's gender. <em>son père</em> is <em>his father</em> or <em>her father</em> — French does not care. What decides is that <em>père</em> is masculine.<br><br>So a woman says <strong>son mari</strong> and a man says <strong>sa femme</strong>.","items":[["Marie parle de son père.","ma-REE parl duh sohn PAIR","Marie talks about her father."],["Paul parle de son père.","pol parl duh sohn PAIR","Paul talks about his father. — identical"],["Marie parle de sa mère.","ma-REE parl duh sa MAIR","Marie talks about her mother."],["Paul parle de sa mère.","pol parl duh sa MAIR","Paul talks about his mother. — identical"]]},{"name":"Ma devient mon devant une voyelle","note":"Before a feminine word starting with a vowel or silent h, <strong>ma → mon, ta → ton, sa → son</strong>. It is purely for the sound — the noun is still feminine.","items":[["une amie → mon amie","moh na-MEE","my friend (f) — not ma amie"],["une adresse → mon adresse","moh na-DRESS","my address"],["une école → ton école","toh nay-KOL","your school"],["une histoire → son histoire","soh nees-TWAHR","his / her story"]]},{"name":"Notre, votre, leur — un seul mot au singulier","note":"These three don't change for gender at all. Only the plural moves: <strong>nos, vos, leurs</strong>.","cols":"two","items":[["notre maison","NOT-ruh may-ZOHN","our house"],["notre jardin","NOT-ruh zhar-DAN","our garden"],["nos enfants","no zahn-FAHN","our children"],["votre nom","VOT-ruh NOHN","your surname"],["vos coordonnées","vo ko-or-do-NAY","your contact details"],["leur fille","lur FEE-yuh","their daughter"],["leurs amis","lur za-MEE","their friends"]]},{"name":"En pratique","items":[["Quel est votre nom ? — Mon nom est Martin.","kel ay VOT-ruh NOHN — mohn nohn ay mar-TAN","What's your surname? — My surname is Martin."],["C'est ma sœur et son mari.","say ma SUR ay sohn ma-REE","This is my sister and her husband."],["Voici mes parents et leurs amis.","vwa-SEE may pa-RAHN ay lur za-MEE","Here are my parents and their friends."],["Mon adresse mail et mon numéro de téléphone.","moh na-DRESS mail ay mohn new-may-RO duh tay-lay-FON","My email address and my phone number."],["Ta langue maternelle, c'est quoi ?","ta lahng ma-tair-NELL, say KWAH","What's your mother tongue?"]]}]},{"id":"tn-present","label":"Le temps","name":"Le présent","summary":"What is happening now, what is generally true, and what is about to happen. Three verb families, plus the irregulars you cannot avoid.","art":null,"groups":[{"name":"Les trois groupes","note":"French verbs fall into three families by their infinitive ending. The <strong>-er</strong> group is by far the biggest — around 90% of all verbs — and completely regular.","cols":"two","items":[["1er groupe : -er — parler, aimer, habiter","par-LAY, ay-MAY, a-bee-TAY","regular, the huge majority"],["2e groupe : -ir — finir, choisir, réussir","fee-NEER, shwa-ZEER, ray-ew-SEER","regular, adds -iss- in the plural"],["3e groupe : -re, -oir, irréguliers — prendre, voir, faire","PRAHN-druh, VWAHR, FAIR","irregular, learn one by one"]]},{"name":"1er groupe — parler","cols":"three","items":[["je parle","zhuh PARL","I speak"],["tu parles","tew PARL","you speak"],["il parle","eel PARL","he speaks"],["nous parlons","noo par-LOHN","we speak"],["vous parlez","voo par-LAY","you speak"],["ils parlent","eel PARL","they speak"]]},{"name":"2e groupe — finir","cols":"three","note":"The giveaway is <strong>-iss-</strong> in the three plural forms.","items":[["je finis","zhuh fee-NEE","I finish"],["tu finis","tew fee-NEE","you finish"],["il finit","eel fee-NEE","he finishes"],["nous finissons","noo fee-nee-SOHN","we finish"],["vous finissez","voo fee-nee-SAY","you finish"],["ils finissent","eel fee-NEESS","they finish"]]},{"name":"Les irréguliers indispensables","cols":"two","items":[["aller : je vais, tu vas, il va, nous allons, vous allez, ils vont","zhuh VAY … eel VOHN","to go"],["faire : je fais, tu fais, il fait, nous faisons, vous faites, ils font","zhuh FAY … noo fuh-ZOHN … eel FOHN","to do, to make"],["prendre : je prends, nous prenons, ils prennent","zhuh PRAHN … eel PREN","to take"],["venir : je viens, nous venons, ils viennent","zhuh vee-AN … eel vee-EN","to come"],["pouvoir : je peux, nous pouvons, ils peuvent","zhuh PUH … eel PUV","to be able to"],["vouloir : je veux, nous voulons, ils veulent","zhuh VUH … eel VUL","to want"],["devoir : je dois, nous devons, ils doivent","zhuh DWAH … eel DWAHV","to have to"],["savoir : je sais, nous savons, ils savent","zhuh SAY … eel SAHV","to know"],["voir : je vois, nous voyons, ils voient","zhuh VWAH … eel VWAH","to see"],["dire : je dis, nous disons, vous dites, ils disent","zhuh DEE … voo DEET","to say"]]},{"name":"À quoi sert le présent","items":[["J'habite à Vancouver.","zha-BEET a vahn-koo-VAIR","a permanent situation"],["Je travaille en ce moment.","zhuh tra-VIGH ahn suh mo-MAHN","happening right now"],["Le train part à huit heures.","luh tran par a wee TUR","a timetabled future"],["L'eau bout à cent degrés.","lo boo a sahn duh-GRAY","a general truth"],["Je suis en train de manger.","zhuh swee zahn tran duh mahn-ZHAY","emphasising right now"]]}]},{"id":"tn-passe-compose","label":"Le temps","name":"Le passé composé","summary":"The everyday past tense. Two pieces: a helper verb in the present, plus the past participle — and the rule for which helper to use.","art":null,"groups":[{"name":"La formule","note":"<strong>avoir</strong> or <strong>être</strong> in the present + the <strong>participe passé</strong>. Most verbs take avoir.","items":[["J'ai mangé.","zhay mahn-ZHAY","I ate / I have eaten."],["Je suis allé.","zhuh swee za-LAY","I went."],["Nous avons fini.","noo za-vohn fee-NEE","We finished."],["Elle est partie.","el ay par-TEE","She left."]]},{"name":"Les participes passés","cols":"two","items":[["-er → -é : parler → parlé","par-LAY","spoken"],["-ir → -i : finir → fini","fee-NEE","finished"],["-re → -u : vendre → vendu","vahn-DEW","sold"],["être → été","ay-TAY","been"],["avoir → eu","EW","had"],["faire → fait","FAY","done"],["prendre → pris","PREE","taken"],["voir → vu","VEW","seen"],["venir → venu","vuh-NEW","come"],["mettre → mis","MEE","put"],["écrire → écrit","ay-KREE","written"],["lire → lu","LEW","read"],["boire → bu","BEW","drunk"],["pouvoir → pu","PEW","been able"],["vouloir → voulu","voo-LEW","wanted"],["dire → dit","DEE","said"]]},{"name":"Les verbes avec être","note":"A short, closed list — mostly verbs of coming and going, plus all reflexives. The classic memory aid is <strong>DR &amp; MRS VANDERTRAMP</strong>. With être, the participle <strong>agrees</strong> with the subject.","cols":"two","items":[["aller / venir","a-LAY / vuh-NEER","to go / to come"],["arriver / partir","a-ree-VAY / par-TEER","to arrive / to leave"],["entrer / sortir","ahn-TRAY / sor-TEER","to enter / to go out"],["monter / descendre","mohn-TAY / day-SAHN-druh","to go up / to go down"],["naître / mourir","NET-ruh / moo-REER","to be born / to die"],["rester / tomber","res-TAY / tohm-BAY","to stay / to fall"],["passer / retourner","pa-SAY / ruh-toor-NAY","to pass by / to return"],["tous les verbes pronominaux","too lay vairb pro-no-mee-NO","all reflexive verbs"]]},{"name":"L'accord avec être","note":"Feminine adds <strong>-e</strong>, plural adds <strong>-s</strong>. With <em>avoir</em> there is no agreement with the subject at all.","items":[["Il est allé.","ee lay ta-LAY","He went."],["Elle est allée.","el ay ta-LAY","She went. — same sound"],["Ils sont allés.","eel sohn ta-LAY","They went. (m)"],["Elles sont allées.","el sohn ta-LAY","They went. (f)"],["Elle s'est levée tôt.","el say luh-VAY TOH","She got up early. — reflexive"],["Elle a mangé.","el a mahn-ZHAY","She ate. — avoir, no agreement"]]},{"name":"La négation","note":"The <strong>ne … pas</strong> wraps around the <em>helper</em>, not the participle.","items":[["Je n'ai pas mangé.","zhuh nay pah mahn-ZHAY","I didn't eat."],["Il n'est pas venu.","eel nay pah vuh-NEW","He didn't come."],["Nous ne sommes pas sortis.","noo nuh som pah sor-TEE","We didn't go out."]]}]},{"id":"tn-imparfait","label":"Le temps","name":"L'imparfait","summary":"The other past. Used for description, habit and background — and the one tense with no exceptions in its endings.","art":null,"groups":[{"name":"Comment le former","note":"Take the <strong>nous</strong> form of the present, drop <strong>-ons</strong>, add the endings. This works for every verb in the language except <em>être</em>.","cols":"two","items":[["nous parlons → parl- → je parlais","zhuh par-LAY","I was speaking"],["nous finissons → finiss- → je finissais","zhuh fee-nee-SAY","I was finishing"],["nous prenons → pren- → je prenais","zhuh pruh-NAY","I was taking"],["nous faisons → fais- → je faisais","zhuh fuh-ZAY","I was doing"],["être → ét- → j'étais","zhay-TAY","I was — the one exception"]]},{"name":"Les terminaisons","cols":"three","items":[["je parlais","zhuh par-LAY","-ais"],["tu parlais","tew par-LAY","-ais"],["il parlait","eel par-LAY","-ait"],["nous parlions","noo par-lee-OHN","-ions"],["vous parliez","voo par-lee-AY","-iez"],["ils parlaient","eel par-LAY","-aient"]]},{"name":"Imparfait ou passé composé ?","note":"<strong>Imparfait</strong> = the setting, the habit, the ongoing. <strong>Passé composé</strong> = the event that happened once and moved the story on.","items":[["Il faisait beau.","eel fuh-ZAY BO","The weather was fine. — description"],["Je mangeais quand le téléphone a sonné.","zhuh mahn-ZHAY kahn luh tay-lay-FON a so-NAY","I was eating when the phone rang."],["Quand j'étais petit, j'habitais à Dhaka.","kahn zhay-TAY puh-TEE, zha-bee-TAY a da-KAH","When I was small I lived in Dhaka. — habit"],["Hier, j'ai visité le musée.","ee-AIR, zhay vee-zee-TAY luh mew-ZAY","Yesterday I visited the museum. — single event"],["Elle était fatiguée alors elle est rentrée.","el ay-TAY fa-tee-GAY a-LOR el ay rahn-TRAY","She was tired so she went home. — both, in one sentence"]]}]},{"id":"tn-plus-que-parfait","label":"Le temps","name":"Le plus-que-parfait","summary":"The past before the past — what had already happened when something else took place.","art":null,"groups":[{"name":"La formule","note":"<strong>avoir</strong> or <strong>être</strong> in the <em>imparfait</em> + the past participle. Same helper rules as the passé composé.","cols":"two","items":[["j'avais mangé","zha-VAY mahn-ZHAY","I had eaten"],["tu avais fini","tew a-VAY fee-NEE","you had finished"],["il avait pris","eel a-VAY PREE","he had taken"],["nous étions partis","noo zay-tee-OHN par-TEE","we had left"],["vous étiez arrivés","voo zay-tee-AY a-ree-VAY","you had arrived"],["elles étaient venues","el zay-TAY vuh-NEW","they had come"]]},{"name":"En contexte","items":[["Quand je suis arrivé, il était déjà parti.","kahn zhuh swee za-ree-VAY, eel ay-TAY day-zha par-TEE","When I arrived, he had already left."],["J'avais oublié mon passeport.","zha-vay zoo-blee-AY mohn pas-POR","I had forgotten my passport."],["Elle a dit qu'elle avait visité Paris.","el a dee kel a-VAY vee-zee-TAY pa-REE","She said she had visited Paris."],["déjà / ne … jamais / avant","day-ZHA / nuh … zha-MAY / a-VAHN","already / never / before — its usual companions"]]}]},{"id":"tn-futur-proche","label":"Le temps","name":"Le futur proche","summary":"The easiest future in French, and the one people actually use in speech: going to do something.","art":null,"groups":[{"name":"aller + infinitif","cols":"two","items":[["je vais manger","zhuh vay mahn-ZHAY","I'm going to eat"],["tu vas partir","tew va par-TEER","you're going to leave"],["il va arriver","eel va a-ree-VAY","he's going to arrive"],["nous allons voir","noo za-lohn VWAHR","we're going to see"],["vous allez comprendre","voo za-lay kohm-PRAHN-druh","you're going to understand"],["ils vont commencer","eel vohn ko-mahn-SAY","they're going to start"]]},{"name":"La négation et les expressions de temps","items":[["Je ne vais pas sortir ce soir.","zhuh nuh vay pah sor-TEER suh SWAHR","I'm not going out tonight."],["demain","duh-MAN","tomorrow"],["ce soir","suh SWAHR","tonight"],["la semaine prochaine","lah suh-men pro-SHEN","next week"],["dans deux jours","dahn duh ZHOOR","in two days"],["tout à l'heure","too ta LUR","later today"],["bientôt","bee-an-TO","soon"]]}]},{"id":"tn-futur-simple","label":"Le temps","name":"Le futur simple","summary":"The written and more distant future. One set of endings for every verb — they are the present tense of avoir.","art":null,"groups":[{"name":"Comment le former","note":"Infinitive + endings. For <strong>-re</strong> verbs, drop the final <em>e</em> first. The endings are the same for every verb without exception: <strong>-ai, -as, -a, -ons, -ez, -ont</strong>.","cols":"three","items":[["je parlerai","zhuh par-luh-RAY","I will speak"],["tu parleras","tew par-luh-RAH","you will speak"],["il parlera","eel par-luh-RAH","he will speak"],["nous parlerons","noo par-luh-ROHN","we will speak"],["vous parlerez","voo par-luh-RAY","you will speak"],["ils parleront","eel par-luh-ROHN","they will speak"],["finir → je finirai","zhuh fee-nee-RAY","I will finish"],["prendre → je prendrai","zhuh prahn-DRAY","I will take"],["écrire → j'écrirai","zhay-kree-RAY","I will write"]]},{"name":"Les radicaux irréguliers","note":"A handful of very common verbs change their stem — but they still take the same endings.","cols":"two","items":[["être → je serai","zhuh suh-RAY","I will be"],["avoir → j'aurai","zho-RAY","I will have"],["aller → j'irai","zhee-RAY","I will go"],["faire → je ferai","zhuh fuh-RAY","I will do"],["venir → je viendrai","zhuh vee-an-DRAY","I will come"],["voir → je verrai","zhuh vay-RAY","I will see"],["pouvoir → je pourrai","zhuh poo-RAY","I will be able"],["vouloir → je voudrai","zhuh voo-DRAY","I will want"],["devoir → je devrai","zhuh duh-VRAY","I will have to"],["savoir → je saurai","zhuh so-RAY","I will know"],["il faut → il faudra","eel fo-DRAH","it will be necessary"],["il y a → il y aura","eel ee o-RAH","there will be"]]},{"name":"Proche ou simple ?","items":[["Je vais partir dans cinq minutes.","zhuh vay par-TEER","near, certain, spoken"],["Un jour, je partirai.","uhn zhoor, zhuh par-tee-RAY","distant, more formal"],["Quand j'aurai le temps, je viendrai.","kahn zho-RAY luh TAHN","after quand, French uses the future where English uses the present"]]}]},{"id":"tn-conditionnel","label":"Le temps","name":"Le conditionnel","summary":"For politeness, wishes and hypotheticals — and the single most useful phrase for a beginner: je voudrais.","art":null,"groups":[{"name":"Comment le former","note":"The <strong>future stem</strong> plus the <strong>imparfait endings</strong>. If you know those two, you already know this one.","cols":"three","items":[["je parlerais","zhuh par-luh-RAY","I would speak"],["tu parlerais","tew par-luh-RAY","you would speak"],["il parlerait","eel par-luh-RAY","he would speak"],["nous parlerions","noo par-luh-ree-OHN","we would speak"],["vous parleriez","voo par-luh-ree-AY","you would speak"],["ils parleraient","eel par-luh-RAY","they would speak"]]},{"name":"La politesse — à apprendre tout de suite","note":"This is why the conditional matters at A1: it turns a demand into a request.","items":[["Je voudrais un café, s'il vous plaît.","zhuh voo-DREH uhn ka-FAY","I would like a coffee, please."],["Je voudrais réserver une chambre.","zhuh voo-DREH ray-zair-VAY ewn SHAHM-bruh","I'd like to book a room."],["Pourriez-vous m'aider ?","poo-ree-ay VOO may-DAY","Could you help me?"],["Est-ce que vous auriez une table ?","es-kuh voo zo-ree-AY ewn TAH-bluh","Would you have a table?"],["J'aimerais visiter Paris.","zhem-RAY vee-zee-TAY pa-REE","I would love to visit Paris."],["Ce serait parfait.","suh suh-RAY par-FAY","That would be perfect."]]},{"name":"Si + imparfait → conditionnel","items":[["Si j'avais le temps, je viendrais.","see zha-VAY luh TAHN, zhuh vee-an-DRAY","If I had time, I would come."],["Si j'étais riche, j'achèterais une maison.","see zhay-TAY REESH, zha-shet-RAY ewn may-ZOHN","If I were rich, I'd buy a house."],["On pourrait aller au cinéma.","ohn poo-RAY a-LAY oh see-nay-MAH","We could go to the cinema."]]}]},{"id":"tn-imperatif","label":"Le mode","name":"L'impératif","summary":"Giving instructions, directions and advice — the form you meet constantly in exercise books and on street signs.","art":null,"groups":[{"name":"Trois formes seulement","note":"Built from the present tense with the subject pronoun removed. For <strong>-er</strong> verbs the <em>tu</em> form drops its <strong>-s</strong>.","cols":"three","items":[["Parle !","PARL","Speak! — tu"],["Parlons !","par-LOHN","Let's speak! — nous"],["Parlez !","par-LAY","Speak! — vous"],["Va !","VAH","Go! — note: vas-y with y"],["Allons !","a-LOHN","Let's go!"],["Allez !","a-LAY","Go!"],["Finis !","fee-NEE","Finish!"],["Finissons !","fee-nee-SOHN","Let's finish!"],["Finissez !","fee-nee-SAY","Finish!"]]},{"name":"Les irréguliers","cols":"two","items":[["être → sois, soyons, soyez","SWAH, swa-YOHN, swa-YAY","be"],["avoir → aie, ayons, ayez","AY, ay-OHN, ay-YAY","have"],["savoir → sache, sachons, sachez","SAHSH, sa-SHOHN, sa-SHAY","know"],["vouloir → veuillez","vuh-YAY","kindly (very formal)"]]},{"name":"Dans la vie de tous les jours","cols":"two","items":[["Écoutez !","ay-koo-TAY","Listen!"],["Répétez !","ray-pay-TAY","Repeat!"],["Regardez !","ruh-gar-DAY","Look!"],["Tournez à droite.","toor-NAY a DRWAHT","Turn right."],["Prenez la première rue.","pruh-NAY lah pruh-mee-AIR REW","Take the first street."],["Asseyez-vous.","a-say-YAY VOO","Sit down."],["Ne fumez pas.","nuh few-MAY PAH","Don't smoke."],["N'ayez pas peur.","na-yay pah PUR","Don't be afraid."],["Excusez-moi.","eks-kew-zay MWAH","Excuse me."],["Attendez !","a-tahn-DAY","Wait!"]]}]},{"id":"tn-subjonctif","label":"Le mode","name":"Le subjonctif présent","summary":"Not a tense but a mood — used after certain expressions of wish, emotion, doubt and necessity. Worth recognising early even if you use it later.","art":null,"groups":[{"name":"Comment le former","note":"Take the <strong>ils</strong> form of the present, drop <strong>-ent</strong>, add: <em>-e, -es, -e, -ions, -iez, -ent</em>. It almost always appears after <strong>que</strong>.","cols":"three","items":[["que je parle","kuh zhuh PARL","that I speak"],["que tu parles","kuh tew PARL","that you speak"],["qu'il parle","keel PARL","that he speaks"],["que nous parlions","kuh noo par-lee-OHN","that we speak"],["que vous parliez","kuh voo par-lee-AY","that you speak"],["qu'ils parlent","keel PARL","that they speak"]]},{"name":"Les irréguliers fréquents","cols":"two","items":[["être → que je sois","kuh zhuh SWAH","that I be"],["avoir → que j'aie","kuh ZHAY","that I have"],["aller → que j'aille","kuh ZHIGH","that I go"],["faire → que je fasse","kuh zhuh FAHSS","that I do"],["pouvoir → que je puisse","kuh zhuh PWEESS","that I can"],["savoir → que je sache","kuh zhuh SAHSH","that I know"],["vouloir → que je veuille","kuh zhuh VUH-yuh","that I want"],["il faut → qu'il faille","keel FIGH","that it be necessary"]]},{"name":"Après quelles expressions","items":[["Il faut que je parte.","eel fo kuh zhuh PART","I have to leave."],["Je veux que tu viennes.","zhuh vuh kuh tew vee-EN","I want you to come."],["Il est important que vous compreniez.","eel ay tan-por-TAHN kuh voo kohm-pruh-nee-AY","It's important that you understand."],["Je suis content que tu sois là.","zhuh swee kohn-TAHN kuh tew swah LAH","I'm glad you're here."],["Bien qu'il soit tard…","bee-an keel swah TAR","Although it's late…"],["avant que / pour que / jusqu'à ce que","a-VAHN kuh / poor kuh / zhews-ka suh kuh","before / so that / until"]]}]}]});
